---
/* FTC affiliate disclosure.
 *
 * The rule is that it must be *clear and conspicuous* and near the links —
 * not buried in a footer, not behind a "read more". So this renders above the
 * article body, in normal reading colour rather than muted grey, and says
 * plainly what the arrangement is.
 *
 * Amazon Associates terminates accounts over a missing disclosure, and that
 * termination is usually permanent. Which is why check-posts.mjs fails the
 * build rather than warning.
 */
---
<aside
  class="not-prose mb-10 border-l-2 border-accent pl-5 py-1 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-text/90"
  role="note"
  aria-label="Affiliate disclosure"
>
  <strong class="font-semibold">Heads up:</strong> some links in this post are
  affiliate links. If you buy through one, I may earn a commission at no extra
  cost to you. I only link to things I have actually used or would recommend
  without the link.
</aside>
